# LOG LEVEL DEFINITIONS, since v1.1
# Log levels mentioned here have already been defined in the program. If a new message type is defined, this file will be changed
Level	Type	Description
0	Critical	When a non-ignorable error occurs, the program will output this message to STDERR.
1	Warning	When an ignorable error occurs, the program will output this message to STDOUT.
2	Information, rate 0	Normal information. e.g.: Incoming login request.
3	Information, rate 1	Normal information, but annoying. e.g.: Incoming MOTD request.
